From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Batocera Team <batocera-linux@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Jan 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Do not write the log summary when logging stops

Skip writeSummary(), so no summary CSV file is created.

Taken from batocera.linux, package/batocera/utils/mangohud/006-no-csv-file.patch
(LGPL-3.0-or-later, Copyright The Batocera Team).

diff --git a/src/logging.cpp b/src/logging.cpp
index f542fcfbf021b72e64bd0920b50f6ff1ab44cb41..8eb1edd91fc5133010352d25333e2b0b3bdb51bd 100644
--- a/src/logging.cpp
+++ b/src/logging.cpp
@@ -292,7 +292,8 @@ void Logger::stop_logging() {
   }
 
   if (!m_log_files.empty())
-    writeSummary(m_log_files.back());
+    // Batocera: skip log summary
+    SPDLOG_INFO("");
   else
     SPDLOG_INFO("Can't write summary because m_log_files is empty");
 
